    // Let f(t, i) = E[p^X_t | X_0 = i]
    // f(0, i) = p^i
    // f(t, i) = (1/(i+1)) * sum_{j=0}^{i} f(t-1, j)

    // We only need f(k, e) for each prime factor.
    // Since e can be at most around 50 (since 2^50 > 10^15), and k can be up to 10^4,
